Your pipeline is now architecturally correct, but there is one major design flaw remaining.

The UI is making it look like these are real employee profiles, when they are actually failed fetches.

For example, this card:

Julien Khaleghy
SerpApi | LinkedIn
Current Employee
Confidence: 0.35
implies that you successfully extracted a LinkedIn profile.

But according to your diagnostics:

AUTH_WALL
HTTP 999
No HTML
No Experience
No Education
No Skills
This is not a verified employee profile.

The real problem
Your pipeline currently does:

Search Result
      ↓
Fetch fails
      ↓
Create empty profile
      ↓
Verification
      ↓
AI Enrichment
      ↓
Show as employee
It should instead do:

Search Result
      ↓
Fetch
      ↓
PUBLIC_PROFILE ?
      │
      ├── YES
      │      ↓
      │  Extraction
      │      ↓
      │ Verification
      │      ↓
      │ Employee
      │
      └── NO
             ↓
      Discovery Candidate
             ↓
      Blocked
Those are completely different objects.

Your data model should become
Instead of everything being a NormalizedEmployee

create two types.

DiscoveryCandidate
Contains

name

linkedinUrl

headline

snippet

company

discoveredBy

failureReason

pageType

providerAttempts

status
status

DISCOVERED

FETCH_BLOCKED

PRIVATE

CAPTCHA

AUTH_WALL

REMOVED
Then

VerifiedEmployee
Contains

experience

education

skills

languages

certifications

projects

recommendations

metadata

statistics
Only created after

PageClassifier == PUBLIC_PROFILE
The UI should reflect this
Instead of

Current Employee
Confidence 0.35
show

Discovery Candidate

⚠ Profile could not be verified

Reason:
LinkedIn Authwall

Status:
FETCH_BLOCKED

Available Information

✓ Name

✓ Headline

✓ URL

✓ Search snippet

✗ Experience

✗ Education

✗ Skills

✗ Certifications

✗ Languages
That is honest.

Confidence score is wrong
Currently

